  ⧗:i #6# ⊞ ⧗:nfr ⊞ ⧖:sig
  ⧗:C̵,sig #2# ‹nd› ⧖:C,ssz ⧗:C̵,i #2# ‹nd› ⧖:C,isz
  ⧗:sig ⧗:ssz ⊞ ⧖:from ⧗:i ⧗:isz ⊞ ⧖:to
  ⧗:C̵,from,to ‹einvert› ⧖:C,nf,nt
  ⧗:C̵ ‹len› ⧖:C,r2 ⧗:C̵ ⧗:name ⍆̵ ⧗:sym ⍆̵ ○ ⍆̵ ⧗:f ⍆̵ ⧗:i ⍆̵ ⧗:nf ⍆̵ ⧗:nt ⍆̵ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,r2 ‹efunction›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹einverse› ⸫

⍝ ‹einvert› C from to: the inverse of the ops from … to, as a new range of nodes
⦃
  ⧖:C,from,to
  ⧗:C̵,from,to ‹eunits› ‹qlist› ⧖:C,L
  ⧗:C̵ #5# ‹reg› ⧖:C,ab
  ⧗:C̵ ‹len› ⧖:C,e0 ⧗:e0 ⧗:ab ⊟ ⧖:nf
  ⧗:C̵,L ‹llen› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,L ⧗:n △ ⊟
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,L,i
    ⧗:C̵,L,i ○ ⧗:i △ ⊞ ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼ ⦃ ⧖:C,L,i ⧗:C̵,L,i ‹lget› ‹ewunit› ⧗:L ⧗:i △ ⊟ ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⌁ ⌁
  ‹len› ⧖:C,e1 ⧗:e1 ⧗:ab ⊟ ⧖:nt
  ⧗:C̵,nf,nt
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ⟩ ‹einvert› ⸫

⍝ ‹eunits› C from to: the units of a reversible body, as a queue of [kind op …]:
⍝ 1 ⊝, 2 a call, 3 a value then ⊞ ⊟ ⩡ [3 op next], 4 ⍿⁰ x ≶ ⋔⇋ [4 op o1 o2 o3 and the
⍝ inverted ranges of its three faces, −1 for ⁼ and ∅]
⦃
  ⧖:C,from,to
  ⧗:C̵ ‹qnew› ⧖:C,q
  ⧗:C̵,q,from,to
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,q,i,to
    ⧗:C̵,q,i,to ⧗:i ⧗:to ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼ ⦃ ‹eunit1› ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⌁ ⌁ ⧖:q ⧗:q
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹eunits› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,q,i,to
  ⧗:C̵,i ○ ‹nd› ⧖:C,k
  ⧗:C̵,i #8861# ‹isglyphn› ⧖:C,isneg
  ⧗:C̵,i ‹nextn› ⧖:C,nx
  ⧗:C̵,i ‹isintlit› ⧖:C,lit
  ⧗:C̵,i #9087# ‹isglyphn› ⧖:C,pk
  ⧗:C̵,i ‹ndt› ⧖:C,tok ⧗:C̵,tok #4# ‹tf› ⧖:C,idx
  ⧗:C̵,nx #8862# ‹isglyphn› ⧖:C,g1 ⧗:C̵,nx #8863# ‹isglyphn› ⧖:C,g2 ⧗:C̵,nx #10849# ‹isglyphn› ⧖:C,g3
  ⧗:lit ⧗:pk ⧗:idx ○ ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⊕ ⦄ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⦃ ⊕ ⦄ ⋎ ⋏ ⧗:g1 ⧗:g2 ⋏ ⧗:g3 ⋏ ⋎ ⧗:nx ⧗:to ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⊕ ⦄ ⁼ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⋎ ⧖:upd
  #4# ⧗:upd ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ #3# ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧗:k #2# ᛖ ⧗:k #4# ᛖ ⋏ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ #2# ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧗:isneg ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ △ ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧖:code
  ⧗:C̵,q,i,nx,code ⍿⁰ △ #3# ᛦ ⋔ ⦃ ‹eunitsimple› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ‹eunitrsel› ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,i2
  ⧗:C̵,q,i2,to
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ⟩ ‹eunit1› ⸫
⍝ ⊝, a call or an update: the unit record and the op after it
⦃
  ⧖:C,q,i,nx,code
  ⧗:C̵ ‹len› ⧖:C,u ⧗:C̵ ⧗:code ⍆̵ ⧗:i ⍆̵ ⧗:nx ⍆̵ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,q,u ‹qadd› ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,nx ⧗:code #3# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ‹nextn› ⦄ ∅ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹eunitsimple› ⸫
⍝ ⍿⁰ x ≶ ⋔⇋: invert the block faces first, so the output nodes stay together
⦃
  ⧖:C,q,i,o1
  ⧗:C̵,o1 ‹nextn› ⧖:C,o2 ⧗:C̵,o2 ‹nextn› ⧖:C,o3
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:o3 #3# ⊞ ⧖:C,f0 ⧗:C̵,f0 ‹nextn› ⧖:C,f1 ⧗:C̵,f1 ‹nextn› ⧖:C,f2
  ⧗:C̵,f0 ‹einvface› ⧖:C,a0,b0 ⧗:C̵,f1 ‹einvface› ⧖:C,a1,b1 ⧗:C̵,f2 ‹einvface› ⧖:C,a2,b2
  ⧗:C̵ ‹len› ⧖:C,u
  ⧗:C̵ #4# ⍆̵ ⧗:i ⍆̵ ⧗:o1 ⍆̵ ⧗:o2 ⍆̵ ⧗:o3 ⍆̵ ⧗:a0 ⍆̵ ⧗:b0 ⍆̵ ⧗:a1 ⍆̵ ⧗:b1 ⍆̵ ⧗:a2 ⍆̵ ⧗:b2 ⍆̵ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,q,u ‹qadd›
  ⧗:o3 ‹nextn›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹eunitrsel› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,f
  ⧗:C̵,f ○ ‹nd› ⧖:C,k
  ⧗:C̵,f ⧗:k #9# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ‹brange› ‹einvert› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ #-1# #-1# ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ⟩ ‹einvface› ⸫

⍝ ‹ecopy› C a b: append the tree slots a … b−1 (relative) again
⦃
  ⧖:C,a,b
  ⧗:C̵ #5# ‹reg› ⧖:C,ab
  ⧗:C̵,ab,a,b
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,ab,j,b
    ⧗:C̵,ab,j,b ⧗:j ⧗:b ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼ ⦃ ⧖:C,ab,j,b ⧗:C̵ ⧗:ab ⧗:j ⊞ ‹rd› ⧖:C,x ⧗:C̵ ⧗:x ⍆̵ ⧗:ab ⧗:j △ ⊞ ⧗:b ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⌁ ⌁ ⌁
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹ecopy› ⸫
⍝ ‹ecopyn› C n: append node n (and what it holds) again
⦃ ⧖:C,n ⧗:C̵,n #2# ‹nd› ⧖:C,sz ⧗:C̵,n ⧗:n ⧗:sz ⊞ ‹ecopy› ⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹ecopyn› ⸫
⍝ ‹enode› C kind tok: append a node header with size 3 (patched by ‹eclose›), giving its slot
⦃ ⧖:C,kind,tok ⧗:C̵ ‹len› ⧖:C,e ⧗:C̵ #5# ‹reg› ⧖:C,ab ⧗:C̵ ⧗:kind ⍆̵ ⧗:tok ⍆̵ #3# ⍆̵ ⧗:e ⧗:ab ⊟ ⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹enode› ⸫
⍝ ‹eclose› C n: node n's size covers everything appended since
⦃
  ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵ #5# ‹reg› ⧖:C,ab
  ⧗:C̵ ‹len› ⧖:C,e
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:ab ⧗:n ⊞ #2# ⊞ ⧗:e ⧗:ab ⊟ ⧗:n ⊟ ‹wr›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹eclose› ⸫

⍝ ‹ewunit› C u: append the inverse of one unit
⦃
  ⧖:C,u
  ⧗:C̵,u ○ ‹vf› ⧖:C,code ⧗:C̵,u △ ‹vf› ⧖:C,op
  ⧗:C̵,u,op,code
  ⍿⁰ △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⧖:uu,o ⧗:o ‹ecopyn› ⦄ ⦃
  ⍿⁰ #2# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⧖:uu,o ⧗:o ○ ‹nd› ⧖:k ⧗:o △ ‹nd› ⧖:t #4# ⧗:k #4# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ #2# ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧖:nk ⧗:nk,t ‹enode› ⌁ ⦄ ⦃
  #3# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⧖:uu,o ⧗:o ‹ecopyn› ⧗:uu #2# ‹vf› ⧖:nx ⧗:nx △ ‹nd› ⧖:t #18# ⧗:t ‹enode› ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ‹ewrsel› ⦄ ⁼ ⦄ ⁼ ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹ewunit› ⸫
⍝ ⍿⁰ x ≶ ⋔⇋ F₀ F₊ F₋ ⦃A⦄  ⟶  ⍿⁰ A ⋔⇋ F₀⁻¹ F₊⁻¹ F₋⁻¹ ⦃x ≶⦄
⦃
  ⧖:C,u
  ⧗:C̵,u △ ‹vf› ⧖:C,p0 ⧗:C̵,u #2# ‹vf› ⧖:C,o1 ⧗:C̵,u #3# ‹vf› ⧖:C,o2 ⧗:C̵,u #4# ‹vf› ⧖:C,o3
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:o3 #3# ⊞ ⧖:C,f0 ⧗:C̵,f0 ‹nextn› ⧖:C,f1 ⧗:C̵,f1 ‹nextn› ⧖:C,f2 ⧗:C̵,f2 ‹nextn› ⧖:C,ab
  ⧗:C̵,p0 ‹ecopyn›
  ⧗:ab ‹brange› ‹ecopy›
  ⧗:o3 △ ‹nd› ⧖:C,rt
  ⧗:C̵ #11# ⧗:rt ‹enode› ⧖:C,h
  ⧗:C̵,u,f0 #5# ‹ewface› ⧗:u,f1 #7# ‹ewface› ⧗:u,f2 #9# ‹ewface›
  #9# ⧗:rt ‹enode› ⧖:C,bh
  ⧗:C̵,o1 ‹ecopyn› ⧗:o2 ‹ecopyn› ⧗:bh ‹eclose› ⧗:h ‹eclose›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹ewrsel› ⸫
⍝ ‹ewface› C u f k: face f, inverted when it is a block (its range in u's fields k, k+1)
⦃
  ⧖:C,u,f,k
  ⧗:C̵,u,k ‹vf› ⧖:C,a ⧗:C̵ ⧗:u ⧗:k △ ⊞ ‹vf› ⧖:C,b
  ⧗:C̵,f,a,b ⧗:a #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ‹ecopyn› ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:ff,aa,bb ⧗:ff △ ‹nd› ⧖:t #9# ⧗:t ‹enode› ⧖:bh ⧗:aa,bb ‹ecopy› ⧗:bh ‹eclose› ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹ewface› ⸫

⍝ ‹eqlit› C q s: append the literal s to q
⦃ ⧖:C,q,s ⧗:C̵ ‹sbeg› ⧖:C,e ⧗:C̵,e,s̵ ‹sapl› ⧗:q,e ‹qadd› ⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ʃ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹eqlit› ⸫
⍝ ‹eqcat› C q r: append the values of queue r to q
⦃
  ⧖:C,q,r
  ⧗:C̵,r ‹rd› ⧖:C,nd
  ⧗:C̵,q,nd
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,q,nd
    ⧗:C̵,q,nd ⧗:nd #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:C,q,nd ⧗:C̵ ⧗:nd △ ⊞ ‹rd› ⧖:C,v ⧗:C̵,q,v ‹qadd› ⧖:C ⧗:C̵,nd ‹rd› ⧖:C,nx ⧗:C̵,q,nx ⊕ ⦄ ⁼
  ⦄
  ⌁ ⌁
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹eqcat› ⸫

⍝ ‹eir› C debug: the module's LLVM IR, as a queue of lines
⦃
  ⧖:C,debug
  ⧗:C̵,debug ‹eregs› ‹efns›
  %%!ᛟ%% ‹efind› #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ #-1# ‹eerr› $a program needs an entry point ᛟ ⟨⊸⟩$ ⎙̵ ‹die› ⦄ ∅ ⁼
  ‹efuns›
  ‹qnew› ⧖:C,q
  ⧗:C̵,q $; generated by trithc (s1)\n%trith.arr = type { ptr, i64, i64 }\ndeclare ptr @trith_arr_new(i64, i64)\ndeclare ptr @trith_arr_push(ptr, i64)\ndeclare void @trith_arr_free(ptr, i64)\ndeclare void @trith_print_str_ref(ptr)$ ‹eqlit›
  #38# ‹reg› ⧖:C,r ⧗:C̵,q,r ‹eqcat›
  ⧗:q $declare ptr @trith_str_new(ptr, i64)\ndeclare void @trith_str_free(ptr)\ndeclare void @trith_print_str(ptr)\ndeclare void @trith_print_i64(i64)\ndeclare void @trith_print_f64(double)$ ‹eqlit›
  ⧗:q $declare void @trith_loop_failed()\ndeclare void @trith_reversal_failed()\ndeclare void @trith_collapse_empty()\ndeclare void @trith_entry_failed()\ndeclare void @llvm.assume(i1)\ndeclare void @llvm.trap()$ ‹eqlit›
  #29# ‹reg› ⧖:C,g ⧗:C̵,q,g ‹eqcat› #28# ‹reg› ⧖:C,l ⧗:C̵,q,l ‹eqcat›
  ⧗:q $\ndeclare void @trith_set_args(i32, ptr)\ndefine i32 @main(i32 %argc, ptr %argv) {\nentry:\n  call void @trith_set_args(i32 %argc, ptr %argv)$ ‹eqlit›
  %%!ᛟ%% ‹efind› △ ‹vf› ⧖:C,es
  ⧗:C̵ %%!ᛟ%% ‹efind› #3# ‹vf› #2# ‹vf› ‹llen› ⧖:C,eo
  ⧗:C̵,es ⧗:eo ○ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⧖:s %%  call void {s}()\n  ret i32 0%% ⦄
    ⦃ ⧖:s %%  %r = call i1 {s}()\n  br i1 %r, label %ok, label %bad\nok:\n  ret i32 0\nbad:\n  call void @trith_entry_failed()\n  ret i32 27%% ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,ep
  ⧗:C̵,q,ep ‹qadd›
  ⧗:q $}\n!0 = !{!"trith tbaa"}\n!1 = !{!"trith.len", !0, i64 0}\n!2 = !{!"trith.data", !0, i64 0}\n!3 = !{!"trith.elem", !0, i64 0}\n!4 = !{!1, !1, i64 0}\n!5 = !{!2, !2, i64 0}\n!6 = !{!3, !3, i64 0}$ ‹eqlit›
  ⧗:q
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹eir› ⸫
⍝ ‹egen› C debug: print the module's LLVM IR
⦃ ‹eir› ‹eprintq› ⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹egen› ⸫

⍝ ‹eglue› C includes: the C text of the FFI wrappers, as a queue of lines (empty without bindings)
⦃
  ⧖:C,includes
  ⧗:C̵ ‹qnew› ⧖:C,q
  ⧗:C̵ #37# ‹reg› ⧖:C,gq ⧗:C̵ ⧗:gq #2# ⊞ ‹rd› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,q,gq,includes ⧗:n ○ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ‹eglue1› ⦄ ⁼
  ⧗:q
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹eglue› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,q,gq,includes
  ⧗:C̵,q $/* FFI glue generated by trithc: the C compiler sees the real prototypes */\n#include <fcntl.h>\n#include <math.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <time.h>\n#include <unistd.h>$ ‹eqlit›
  ⧗:q,includes ‹eqcat›
  ⧗:q $typedef struct { char *ptr; int64_t len; int64_t cap; } TrithStr;\nconst char *trith_str_cstr(TrithStr *s);\nTrithStr *trith_str_from_cstr(const char *c);\nvoid trith_str_free(TrithStr *s);$ ‹eqlit›
  ⧗:q $int64_t trith_argc(void);\nconst char *trith_arg(int64_t i);\nconst char *trith_read_file(const char *path);\nint64_t trith_write_file(const char *path, const char *data);$ ‹eqlit›
  ⧗:q,gq ‹eqcat›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹eglue1› ⸫

⍝ ‹eqtext› C q s: the lines of q appended to the text s, each followed by a newline (UTF-8)
⦃
  ⧖:C,q,s
  ⧗:C̵,q ‹rd› ⧖:C,nd
  ⧗:C̵,s̵,nd
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,s,nd
    ⧗:C̵,s̵,nd ⧗:nd #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:C,s,nd ⧗:C̵ ⧗:nd △ ⊞ ‹rd› ⧖:C,v ⧗:C̵,s̵,v ‹estext› #10# ⍆̵ ⧖:C,s2 ⧗:C̵,nd ‹rd› ⧖:C,nx ⧗:C̵,s2̵,nx ⊕ ⦄ ⁼
  ⦄
  ⌁
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ʃ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ʃ⟩ ‹eqtext› ⸫
⍝ ‹estext› C s v: heap string v appended to the text s
⦃
  ⧖:C,s,v
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:v △ ⊞ ‹rd› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,s̵ ⧗:v #2# ⊞ ⧗:v #2# ⊞ ⧗:n ⊞
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,s,j,end
    ⧗:C̵,s̵,j,end ⧗:j ⧗:end ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼
      ⦃ ⧖:C,s,j,end ⧗:C̵,j ‹rd› ⧖:C,c ⧗:C̵,s̵ ⧗:c ⧗:c #127# ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⍆̵ ⦄ ⦃ ᚦ ⦄ ⦃ ⍆̵ ⦄ ⧖:C,s2 ⧗:C̵,s2̵ ⧗:j △ ⊞ ⧗:end ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⌁ ⌁
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ʃ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ʃ⟩ ‹estext› ⸫

⍝ ---- predicates: what ⍤, ⊨, ⋔⇋ and ⟜ see is copies of classical values and shadows of quantum ones

⦃
  ⧖:C,vals
  ⧗:C̵ ‹qnew› ⧖:C,q
  ⧗:C̵,vals ‹llen› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,vals,q ○ ⧗:n
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,vals,q,i,n
    ⧗:C̵,vals,q,i,n ⧗:i ⧗:n ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼
      ⦃ ⧖:C,vals,q,i,n ⧗:C̵,vals,i ‹lget› ⧖:C,e ⧗:C̵,e ‹ety› ⧖:C,t ⧗:C̵,t ‹tcopy› ⧖:C,cp
        ⧗:C̵,e,t ⧗:cp ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:ee,tt ⧗:ee ‹ev› ⧖:v #10199# ⧗:tt ‹spre› ⧖:st ⧗:st,v #-1# ‹ent› ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,e2
        ⧗:C̵,q,e2 ‹qadd› ⧗:vals,q ⧗:i △ ⊞ ⧗:n ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⌁ ⌁ ⧖:q ⌁ ⧗:q ‹qlist›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹eshadows› ⸫
⍝ ‹epred› C b vals: run block node b on vals, giving its trit (−1 if it never finishes)
⦃
  ⧖:C,b,vals
  ⧗:C̵,b,vals ‹esubb› ⧖:C,R,st,dead
  ⧗:C̵,R ⧗:dead ○ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ○ ‹lget› ‹ev› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ #-1# ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹epred› ⸫

⍝ x ⦃pred⦄ ⊨ → ◌T whose flag is pred = ⊕
⦃
  ⧖:C,op,S,strand,dead,prev,to
  ⧗:C̵,S △ ‹epop› ⧖:C,S2,pv
  ⧗:C̵,pv ○ ‹lget› ‹eunwrap› ⧖:C,x
  ⧗:C̵,x ‹l1› ‹eshadows› ⧖:C,pvals
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:op #3# ⊞ ⧗:pvals ‹epred› ⧖:C,t
  ⧗:C̵ %%icmp eq i8 {t}, 1%% ‹edef› ⧖:C,ok
  ⧗:C̵,x ‹ety› ⧖:C,xt ⧗:C̵,x ‹ev› ⧖:C,xv
  ⧗:C̵ #9676# ⧗:xt ‹spre› ⧖:C,rt
  ⧗:C̵,rt,xv,ok ‹ent› ⧖:C,e
  ⧗:C̵,S2,e ‹lpush› ⧗:strand,dead △
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ⟩ ‹el_attest› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,op,S,strand,dead,prev,to
  ⧗:C̵,op,to ‹isattest› ⧖:C,at
  ⧗:C̵,op,S,strand,dead,prev,to ⧗:at ⋔ ⦃ ‹el_attest› ⦄ ⦃ ‹el_quotation› ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ⟩ ‹el_quote› ⸫
⍝ a quotation: nothing at run time (§9.5)
⦃
  ⧖:C,op,S,strand,dead,prev,to
  ⧗:C̵,op ‹ndt› ⧖:C,tok ⧗:C̵,tok ‹qtype› ⧖:C,qt
  ⧗:C̵ #48# ‹reg› ⧖:C,zero
  ⧗:C̵,qt,zero #-1# ‹ent› ⧖:C,e
  ⧗:C̵,S,e ‹lpush› ⧗:strand,dead ○
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ⟩ ‹el_quotation› ⸫
⍝ ⍎: the quotation's body, inlined on this stack (§9.5)
⦃
  ⧖:C,op,S,strand,dead,prev,to
  ⧗:C̵,S △ ‹epop› ⧖:C,S2,qv
  ⧗:C̵,qv ○ ‹lget› ‹ety› ⧖:C,qt
  ⧗:C̵,qt ‹qget› ⧖:C,qn
  ⧗:C̵ #61# ‹reg› ⧖:C,vw0 ⧗:C̵ #61# ○ ‹wr› ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:qn #3# ⊞ ⧗:S2 ‹esubb› ⧖:C,R,qst,qdead
  ⧗:C̵ #61# ⧗:vw0 ‹wr› ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,R,strand,qdead ○
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ⟩ ‹el_apply› ⸫

⍝ ‹ersel› C op S c k dead: ⋔⇋ checks its exit assertion against the condition (§10)
⦃
  ⧖:C,op,S,c,k,dead
  ⧗:C̵,op,S,c ⧗:k #11# ᛖ ⧗:dead ○ ᛖ ⋎ ⋔ ⦃ ‹ersel1› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹ersel› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,op,S,c
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:op #3# ⊞ ‹nextn› ‹nextn› ‹nextn› ⧖:C,ab
  ⧗:C̵,S ‹llen› ⧖:C,n ⧗:C̵,S ⧗:n △ ⊟ ‹lget› ⧖:C,topv
  ⧗:C̵,topv ‹l1› ⧖:C,tv
  ⧗:C̵,ab,tv ‹epred› ⧖:C,at
  ⧗:C̵,c ‹ev› ⧖:C,cv
  ⧗:C̵ %%icmp eq i8 {at}, {cv}%% ‹edef› ⧖:C,same
  ⧗:C̵ ‹elabel› ⧖:C,lgood ⧗:C̵ ‹elabel› ⧖:C,lbad
  ⧗:C̵,same,lgood,lbad ‹ebr2› ⧗:lbad ‹estart›
  %%call void @trith_reversal_failed()%% ‹eemit› %%unreachable%% ‹eemit›
  ⧗:lgood ‹estart›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹ersel1› ⸫

⍝ ⍤ⁿ: proved and erased when its values are known, else assumed (or trapped with --debug, §12)
⦃
  ⧖:C,op,S,strand,dead,prev,to
  ⧗:C̵,op ‹ndt› ⧖:C,tok
  ⧗:C̵,tok #4# ‹tf› ⧖:C,pn
  ⧗:C̵,S ‹llen› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,S ⧗:n ⧗:pn ⊟ ⧗:n ‹lslice› ‹eshadows› ⧖:C,vals
  ⧗:C̵,vals ‹etovals› ⧖:C,kv
  ⧗:C̵ ⧗:op #3# ⊞ ⧖:C,b
  ⧗:C̵,b,vals,kv,tok ⧗:kv #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ‹epred› ‹eassume› ⦄ ⦃ ‹eprove› ⦄ ⁼
  ⧗:S,strand,dead ○
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ⟩ ‹el_prayer› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,t
  ⧗:C̵ %%icmp eq i8 {t}, 1%% ‹edef› ⧖:C,c
  ⧗:C̵ #34# ‹reg› ⧖:C,debug
  ⧗:C̵,c ⧗:debug △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ‹etrapunless› ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:cc %%call void @llvm.assume(i1 {cc})%% ‹eemit› ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹eassume› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,c
  ⧗:C̵ ‹elabel› ⧖:C,lok ⧗:C̵ ‹elabel› ⧖:C,lbad
  ⧗:C̵,c,lok,lbad ‹ebr2› ⧗:lbad ‹estart›
  %%call void @llvm.trap()%% ‹eemit› %%unreachable%% ‹eemit›
  ⧗:lok ‹estart›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹etrapunless› ⸫
⍝ the prayer's values are known: decide it now
⦃
  ⧖:C,b,vals,kv,tok
  ⧗:C̵ ‹evnew›
  ⧗:b,kv ‹evblockn› ⧖:C,PS
  ⧗:C̵,tok ‹evdie› ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,PS ○ ‹lget› △ ‹vf› ⧖:C,verdict
  ⧗:C̵,tok ⧗:verdict ○ ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ‹eerr› $doubt: this prayer is neither true nor false (it yields ⦶; §12)$ ⎙̵ ‹die› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄
    ⦃ ‹eerr› $blasphemy: this prayer is false for the values it is given (§12)$ ⎙̵ ‹die› ⦄
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧⟩ ‹eprove› ⸫

⍝ ---- compile-time values: an entry with a known value carries c

⍝ ‹etoval› C e: the evaluator value [ty n ok role hasn] of entry e, or −1 when not known
⦃
  ⧖:C,e
  ⧗:C̵,e ‹ety› ⧖:C,ty ⧗:C̵,e ‹eok› ⧖:C,ok ⧗:C̵,e #4# ‹vf› ⧖:C,hc ⧗:C̵,e #5# ‹vf› ⧖:C,c
  ⧗:C̵,ty ‹efailty› ⧖:C,f ⧗:C̵,ty #15# ‹tis› ⧖:C,bare
  ⧗:C̵ #46# ‹etx› ⧖:C,yes ⧗:C̵ #47# ‹etx› ⧖:C,no
  ⍝ 0 unknown, 1 a failed ◌, 2 a bare ◌ that holds, 3 the known value c
  ○ ⧗:hc △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ #3# ⦄ ∅ ⁼
  ⧗:f ⧗:ok ⧗:yes ᛖ ‹not› ⋎ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ○ ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧗:f ⧗:bare ⋎ ⧗:ok ⧗:yes ᛖ ⋎ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ #2# ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧗:f ⧗:ok ⧗:no ᛖ ⋎ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ △ ⦄ ∅ ⁼ ⧖:k
  ⧗:C̵,ty,c,k
  ⍿⁰ ○ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ #-1# ⦄ ⦃
  ⍿⁰ △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ○ ○ ○ ‹evval› ⦄ ⦃
  #2# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ○ ○ △ ‹evval› ⦄ ⦃ △ △ ‹evval› ⦄ ⁼ ⦄ ⁼ ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹etoval› ⸫
⍝ ‹evval› C ty n hasn ok: a new value (no role)
⦃ ⧖:C,ty,n,hasn,ok ⧗:C̵ ‹len› ⧖:C,v ⧗:C̵ ⧗:ty ⍆̵ ⧗:n ⍆̵ ⧗:ok ⍆̵ #-1# ⍆̵ ⧗:hasn ⍆̵ ⧗:v ⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹evval› ⸫
⍝ ‹etovals› C es: the values of every entry, or −1 if one is not known
⦃
  ⧖:C,es
  ⧗:C̵ ‹qnew› ⧖:C,q
  ⧗:C̵,es ‹llen› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,es,q ○ ⧗:n ⦶
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,es,q,i,n,all
    ⧗:C̵,es,q,i,n,all ⧗:i ⧗:n ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼
      ⦃ ⧖:C,es,q,i,n,all ⧗:C̵,es,i ‹lget› ‹etoval› ⧖:C,v ⧗:C̵,q,v ‹qadd› ⧗:es,q ⧗:i △ ⊞ ⧗:n ⧗:all ⧗:v #-1# ᛖ ‹not› ⋎ ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⧖:C,es,q,i,n,all
  ⧗:C̵,q ⧗:all ⋔ ⦃ ‹qlist› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ #-1# ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹etovals› ⸫
⍝ ‹efromval› C val: an entry for an evaluator value
⦃
  ⧖:C,val
  ⧗:C̵,val ○ ‹vf› ⧖:C,ty ⧗:C̵,val △ ‹vf› ⧖:C,n ⧗:C̵,val #2# ‹vf› ⧖:C,ok ⧗:C̵,val #4# ‹vf› ⧖:C,hn
  ⧗:C̵,ty ‹efailty› ⧖:C,f
  ⧗:C̵,ty,n,ok,hn ⧗:f ⋔ ⦃ ‹efromfail› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ⧖:t,nn %%!{#nn}%% ⧖:v ⧗:t,v,nn ○ ‹entc› ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹efromval› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,ty,n,ok,hn
  ⧗:C̵,ok △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ #46# ‹etx› ⦄ ⦃ #47# ‹etx› ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,okt
  ⧗:C̵,ty #15# ‹tis› ⧖:C,bare
  ⧗:C̵,ty ‹stail› ⧖:C,bt ⧗:C̵,bt ‹ellty› ⧖:C,blt
  ⧗:C̵,blt,n ⧗:hn △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⧖:l,nn %%!{#nn}%% ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ‹ezero› ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,v
  ⧗:ok △ ᛖ ⧗:hn △ ᛖ ⋎ ⋔ ⦃ △ ⦄ ⦃ ○ ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:hasc
  ⧗:C̵,ty,v,okt,hasc,n,bare ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ⧖:t,vv,o ⧗:t #-1# ⧗:o ‹ent› ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:t,vv,o,hc,nn ⧗:t,vv,o #-1# ⧗:hc,nn ○ #-1# #-1# #-1# #-1# ‹entx› ⦄ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹efromfail› ⸫

⍝ ---- past tense (§9.2): the call already happened, so it is evaluated now

⦃
  ⧖:C,S,f,tok
  ⧗:C̵,f ‹rd› ⧖:C,nm
  ⧗:C̵ ‹qnew› ⧖:C,seen
  ⧗:C̵,nm,seen ‹evpure› ⧖:C,pure
  ⧗:C̵,tok,nm ⧗:pure ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⌁ ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:tk,n ⧗:tk ‹eerr› $a past-tense call needs a pure function, and $ ⎙̵ ⧗:n ‹spr› $ is not (or is beyond s1's evaluator: only ℤ and ŧ code)$ ⎙̵ ‹die› ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,f #3# ‹vf› ⧖:C,fr ⧗:C̵,fr △ ‹vf› ⧖:C,ins
  ⧗:C̵,ins ‹llen› ⧖:C,k
  ⧗:C̵,S,k ‹epop› ⧖:C,S2,args
  ⧗:C̵,args ‹etovals› ⧖:C,vals
  ⧗:C̵,tok ⧗:vals #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ‹eerr› $the past cannot depend on the present: every argument of a past-tense call must be known at compile time (§9.2)$ ⎙̵ ‹die› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵ ‹evnew› ⧖:C
  ⍝ arguments may be ◌ values; unwrap where the parameter is not ◌
  ⧗:C̵ ‹qnew› ⧖:C,q
  ⧗:C̵,vals,ins,q ○ ⧗:k
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,vals,ins,q,i,k
    ⧗:C̵,vals,ins,q,i,k ⧗:i ⧗:k ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼
      ⦃ ⧖:C,vals,ins,q,i,k ⧗:C̵,vals,i ‹lget› ⧖:C,v ⧗:C̵,ins,i ‹lget› ‹efailty› ⧖:C,pf
        ⧗:C̵,v ⧗:pf ⋔ ⦃ ⦄ ⦃ ‹evunwrap› ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,u ⧗:C̵,q,u ‹qadd› ⧗:vals,ins,q ⧗:i △ ⊞ ⧗:k ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵ #50# ‹reg› ⧖:C,failed
  ⧗:C̵,tok ⧗:failed △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ‹eerr› $a past-tense call received a failed argument$ ⎙̵ ‹die› ⦄ ⦃ ⌁ ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,q ‹qlist› ⧖:C,uv
  ⧗:C̵,f,uv ‹evcall› ⧖:C,res
  ⧗:C̵,tok ‹evdie› ⧖:C
  ⧗:C̵,res ‹llen› ⧖:C,nr
  ⧗:C̵,S2,res ○ ⧗:nr
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,S,res,i,n
    ⧗:C̵,S,res,i,n ⧗:i ⧗:n ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼
      ⦃ ⧖:C,S,res,i,n ⧗:C̵,res,i ‹lget› ‹efromval› ⧖:C,e ⧗:C̵,S,e ‹lpush› ⧖:C,S3 ⧗:C̵,S3,res ⧗:i △ ⊞ ⧗:n ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⧖:C,S,res,i,n ⧗:C̵,S
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹epast› ⸫

⍝ ---- superpositions (§8.3–§8.5): one SSA value per alternative, plus i1 flags live and
⍝ neg (phase −). Constant flags fold away in LLVM.

⦃ ⧖:C,ty,sl,lv,ng ⧗:C̵,ty #-1# #-1# #-1# ○ ○ ○ ⧗:sl,lv,ng #-1# ‹entx› ⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹epsient› ⸫
⍝ ‹epsiof› C e: a classical entry as a one-alternative superposition
⦃
  ⧖:C,e
  ⧗:C̵,e #7# ‹vf› ⧖:C,sl
  ⧗:C̵,e ⧗:sl #-1# ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ‹epsiof1› ⦄ ∅ ⁼
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹epsiof› ⸫
⦃
  ⧖:C,e
  ⧗:C̵,e ‹ety› ⧖:C,t ⧗:C̵,e ‹ev› ⧖:C,v
  ⧗:C̵ △ ⧗:t ‹psitype› ⧖:C,pt
  ⧗:C̵,v ‹l1› ⧖:C,sl ⧗:C̵ #46# ‹etx› ‹l1› ⧖:C,lv ⧗:C̵ #47# ‹etx› ‹l1› ⧖:C,ng
  ⧗:C̵,pt,sl,lv,ng ‹epsient›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹epsiof1› ⸫
⍝ ‹ebool› C op a b: an i1 operation (op: 0 and, 1 or, 2 xor)
⦃
  ⧖:C,op,a,b
  ⧗:C̵,a,b ⧗:op ⍿⁰ ○ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ ⧖:x,y %%and i1 {x}, {y}%% ⦄ ⦃ △ ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⧖:x,y %%or i1 {x}, {y}%% ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:x,y %%xor i1 {x}, {y}%% ⦄ ⁼ ⦄ ⁼ ‹edef›
⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ℤ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹ebool› ⸫
⦃ ⧖:C,a ⧗:C̵ #46# ‹etx› ⧖:C,t ⧗:C̵ #2# ⧗:a,t ‹ebool› ⦄ ⟨⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ ⊸ ⟦ℤ⟧ ℤ⟩ ‹enot1› ⸫

⍝ ‹esuper› C a b: a ⫴ b, then interference: equal alternatives with the same phase merge,
⍝ with opposite phases annihilate (§8.4)
⦃
  ⧖:C,a,b
  ⧗:C̵,a ‹epsiof› ⧖:C,A ⧗:C̵,b ‹epsiof› ⧖:C,B
  ⧗:C̵,A #7# ‹vf› ⧖:C,sa ⧗:C̵,B #7# ‹vf› ⧖:C,sb ⧗:C̵,sa,sb ‹lcat› ⧖:C,sl
  ⧗:C̵,A #8# ‹vf› ⧖:C,la ⧗:C̵,B #8# ‹vf› ⧖:C,lb ⧗:C̵,la,lb ‹lcat› ⧖:C,lv
  ⧗:C̵,A #9# ‹vf› ⧖:C,na ⧗:C̵,B #9# ‹vf› ⧖:C,nb ⧗:C̵,na,nb ‹lcat› ⧖:C,ng
  ⧗:C̵,A ‹ety› ‹psibase› ⧖:C,base
  ⧗:C̵,base ‹ellty› ⧖:C,lt
  ⧗:C̵ #43# ‹etx› ⧖:C,dbl
  ⧗:C̵,lt ⧗:lt ⧗:dbl ᛖ ⋔ ⦃ ⌁ %%fcmp oeq double%% ⦄ ⦃ ⧖:l %%icmp eq {l}%% ⦄ ⁼ ⧖:C,eqop
  ⧗:C̵,sl ‹llen› ⧖:C,n
  ⧗:C̵,sl,lv,ng,eqop △ ⧗:n
  ⥀ ⦃
    ⧖:C,sl,lv,ng,eqop,j,n
    ⧗:C̵,sl,lv,ng,eqop,j,n ⧗:j ⧗:n ≶ ⋔ ⦃ ⦶ ⦄ ⁼ ⦃ ‹esuperj› ⊕ ⦄
  ⦄
  ⌁ ⌁ ⌁ ⧖:C,sl,lv,ng
  ⧗:C̵,n,base ‹psitype› ⧖:C,pt
  ⧗:C̵,pt,sl,lv,ng ‹epsient›
